    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting an elite 82.13 efficiency score, he faces Merrill Kelly, whose 5.27 xERA provides a massive window for offensive production. The combination of a favorable platoon advantage and a leadoff spot ensures **Pete Crow-Armstrong** will maximize his stolen base potential\u2014the most vital commodity in our current Roto build. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (76.13) stands as an elite start; while facing a lefty like Framber Valdez typically requires caution, **Junior Caminero** has enough plate discipline and raw power to thrive in the #3 hole, particularly with wind conditions pushing his ceiling higher today. **Lars Nootbaar** (60.62) also cracks the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, as his dynamic platoon edge against Kevin Gausman creates enough value to overcome a challenging matchup against a high-tier arm.\n\nWhile we remain aggressive, we must navigate the risk of high-end starters. **Kyle Schwarber** (50.87) and **Trea Turner** (51.35) are facing the formidable Logan Gilbert; their scores are suppressed by the quality of the opposing arm, but their positional roles at the top of the order keep them in the lineup for their ability to contribute to counting stats despite the efficiency hurdle. The most difficult decision today involved the bench, where **Jacob Gonzalez** narrowly missed the cut with a 42.41 score. While his matchup against Robbie Ray was statistically favorable, the optimizer favored the higher daily ceilings offered by our middle infielders. **Dillon Dingler** also remained on the bench; his 37.53 score was heavily hindered by a poor platoon dynamic against Drew Rasmussen, making him a clear \"below floor\" option we are benched to protect our games-played cap. As always, all lineup spots remain tentative pending official verification, as any shift in the batting order for **Colt Keith** or **Caleb Durbin** could necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their projected efficiency.",
